<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Hindol State</h1><p class="st-meta">1554 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Hindol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the small tributary Garhjat states of Orissa, ruled by a Raja from its hill-ringed seat in the Mahanadi uplands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hindol lay in the forested hills north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanadi">Mahanadi</a>, in today's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dhenkanal-state">Dhenkanal</a> district. Its ruling family's traditions date the state to the mid-16th century, when chiefs from neighbouring houses carved out holdings among the tribal hill country of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Raja ruled a population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odia-language">Oriya</a> peasants and tribal communities, drawing revenue from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> cultivation and forest produce. After the British conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> in 1803 Hindol became one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orissa-tributary-states">Orissa Tributary Mahals</a>, later grouped in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Following widespread popular agitation (the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praja-mandal">Praja Mandal</a> movement) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> states, its ruler signed the merger agreement and Hindol joined the province of Orissa on 1 January 1948.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hindol-state.jpg" alt="Hindol State" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Regierung von Britisch-Indien. Kartograph J. G. Bartholomew (gest. 1920) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DhenkanalKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1554 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hindol</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Odia</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hindol</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1751&amp;focus=hindol-state" aria-label="Hindol State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6976 1424 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hindol State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7296 1680L7364 1601M7296 1680L7364 1602M7296 1680L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7296 1680h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7296 1680h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1751&amp;focus=hindol-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
